+### 3. Qwen3-32B, TP=4, 16K context (H200)
+
+Long-context co-serving: 16K-token inference prompts AND FT samples up to 16K tokens. Validated
+2026-10-12 on 4× H200 (`EXPERIMENTS.md`, lc16k-b). Every batch's loss is lower in epoch 1 than in
+epoch 0, and a 14,867-token sample trains in 9.4 s.
+
+```bash
+cd DeltaServe-vLLM
+ENV=$HOME/miniconda3/envs/dserve-vllm
+# per shell: env-private FlashInfer JIT cache (a stale CUDA-12 cache in ~/.cache/flashinfer
+# crashes sampling with "libcudart.so.12: cannot open") + a CUDA >= 12.9 nvcc for its JIT
+export FLASHINFER_WORKSPACE_BASE=$HOME/.cache/flashinfer-dserve CUDA_HOME=/usr/local/cuda-13.2 \
+       PATH=/usr/local/cuda-13.2/bin:$ENV/bin:$PATH HF_HUB_OFFLINE=1 CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0,1,2,3
+
+# (a) training-only benchmark (no inference traffic); bwd log in eval-tp/output/
+$ENV/bin/python eval-tp/ft_bench_tp.py \
+    --config configs/serving_config_finetuning_qwen3_32b_tp4_16k.yaml \
+    --rps 0 --duration 300 --startup-timeout 2400 --kill-stale
+
+# (b) just bring the server up (inference on :8000, FT in the gaps)
+$ENV/bin/python eval-tp/launch_deltaserve.py \
+    --config configs/serving_config_finetuning_qwen3_32b_tp4_16k.yaml --start-finetuning
+```
+
+- **Startup** takes 3–5 min with a warm compile cache and more than 10 min on a fresh one. Keep
+  `--startup-timeout 2400`; the default of 600 s kills the server mid-compile, and the error
+  surfaces as a misleading Inductor `aten::slice ... SymInt` message.
+- **`gpu_memory_utilization` must stay at 0.42.** vLLM's budget does not include the activation
+  buffers, which are ~58 GB per card at 16K, so anything higher OOMs at KV allocation.
+- **FT data:** `finetune.data_path`, one sample per line, at most 16K tokens. The default
+  `long_ft_corpus.txt` is a test corpus built by `scripts/make_long_ft_corpus.py`.
+- **Served model name:** `llama3`. The launchers' default family tag is a naming quirk; the model
+  is Qwen3-32B. The output files are tagged `llama3_tp4` for the same reason.
+- **Not yet validated:** co-serving under heavy 16K *inference* traffic. The step-time estimator
+  is linear in tokens, so it may under-predict long-prompt TTFT.
+- **Knobs and code changes:** see `VLLM_FORK_CHANGES.md`, "Stage LC".
+
+### 4. RSI-system workloads (ACE Finance) on DeltaServe
+
+[RSI-system](https://github.com/Jianshu-She/RSI-system) turns agent traces into chat JSONL and LoRA-trains Qwen3-32B on
+them. DeltaServe trains on the same files directly. Set `finetune.data_path` to a `.jsonl` file plus
+`finetune.chat_loss_on` / `chat_thinking`; the rendering is token-for-token the offline trainers'. The served model
+can carry YaRN x4 (the backward's RoPE follows it), and the trained adapter is exported as a PEFT directory.
+
+```bash
+# per shell: same env as §3. One 8×H200 node (salloc --no-shell … then srun --jobid=<id> --overlap …)
+CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0,1,2,3 eval-rsi/run_ds_ace.sh formula     # TP=4 training only -> eval-rsi/adapters/formula/final
+CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0,1,2,3 eval-rsi/run_ds_ace.sh finer
+eval-rsi/eval_ace.sh 4 9314 formula ds_formula $PWD/eval-rsi/adapters/formula/final   # their protocol: vLLM 0.31, empty ctx
+eval-rsi/eval_ace.sh 5 9315 formula base_formula                                      # base, same node
+python3 eval-rsi/compare_ace.py formula base ctrl ds                                  # paired sign tests
+```
+
+- Config: `configs/serving_config_finetuning_qwen3_32b_tp4_rsi_ace.yaml` (YaRN model dir, q,k,v,o r16/α32 from
+  `scripts/init_qwen3_lora_adapter.py`, lr 1e-4, 2 epochs, 16K tokens per backward, `chat_loss_on: ace`,
+  `adapter_save_dir`). The driver writes a per-task copy (data path, export dir, bwd log) to `configs/.gen_rsi_ace_<task>.yaml`.
+- Exports: `<adapter_save_dir>/cycle<N>/` every `adapter_save_every` cycles, `latest/`, and `final/` once
+  `num_epochs` epochs are trained. Under TP, rank 0 writes the merged adapter.
+- Result (2026-10-19, `EXPERIMENTS.md` rsi-ace-1): Formula 68.0 → **75.5**, FiNER 61.5 → **71.2** test accuracy; their
+  offline full LoRA scores 75.0 / 68.5. Formula trained in 4 min and FiNER in 7 min on 4 H200s.
+- **End to end on one server** (`eval-rsi/run_rsi_e2e.sh`, config `…_rsi_e2e.yaml`):
+  1. Serve the traffic, keeping traces (`eval-rsi/rsi_traffic.py`).
+  2. Convert the correct traces into SFT rows (`eval-rsi/traces_to_sft.py`) and send them to `POST /ft/ingest`
