+## Stage RSI — RSI-system chat SFT data, YaRN backward RoPE, adapter export (2026-10-19)
+
+All inert by default: a plain-text corpus, a model without rope scaling, and no `adapter_save_dir` all keep the old
+behaviour.
+
+**Chat SFT data (loss on assistant tokens only).**
+- `deltaserve/chat_sft.py` ports the encode functions of RSI-system's trainers: `chat_loss_on` = `last` / `all` (the
+  shared `rsi/finetune/train_lora.py`) or `ace` (the ACE trainer); `chat_thinking` = on / off.
+- `config/finetune.py`: a `.jsonl` `data_path` selects it, configured by `chat_loss_on` and `chat_thinking`.
+- `finetuning_store.py`: `FinetuningSample.loss_spans`; JSONL rows are rendered with the HF tokenizer, which
+  `ft_scheduler._build_tokenize` attaches as `tokenize.tokenizer`.
+
+**Getting the spans to the backward in the runner's write order.** The scheduler's FT order can differ from the
+InputBatch order, so the spans are matched by FT request id:
+- The scheduler passes `reserve(…, req_spans={req_id: spans})`.
+- The runner reports `_ft_req_ids` in write order, through `record_capture(n, lens, req_ids)` or the TP relay tuple
+  `ModelRunnerOutput.finetune_saved = (n, lens, ids)`.
+- The coordinator keeps `sample_spans`, parallel to `sample_lens`, and ships them as `loss_spans` on the trigger:
+  `notify_buffer_full` at TP=1, the relayed command under TP.
+- `bwd_services/base.py` and `common/trainer.py` pass `loss_spans` to `common/head.py:head_backward`, which keeps
+  only the rows predicting span tokens; `n_valid` = the number of target tokens.
+
+**YaRN in the backward RoPE.**
+- `ft_meta.rope_scaling_of`: None, or a YaRN dict. Any other scaling raises.
+- `common/ops.rope_cos_sin(…, scaling)` reuses vLLM's YaRN helpers: frequencies plus `mscale` on cos/sin.
+- Wired into both the trainer and the graph runner. RSI-system serves Qwen3-32B with YaRN x4.
+
+**Adapter export.**
+- `LoraSftTrainerService.export_adapter` writes the fp32 masters as a PEFT directory, with the
+  `adapter_config.json` copied from the source adapter. Under TP the shards are gathered over the children's
+  gloo group (q/k/v B row shards, o A column shards) and rank 0 writes.
+- Triggers: `finetune.adapter_save_dir` / `adapter_save_every` (`cycle<N>/` + `latest/`), plus `final/` once
+  `num_epochs` are trained (`after_cycle` hook in `base.py`).
+
+**Runtime ingest (`POST /ft/ingest`).**
+- `entrypoints/serve/finetune/api_router.py` handles `/ft/ingest`, which makes an EngineCore utility call
+  (`engine_core.call_utility_async`) to `v1/engine/core.py:EngineCore.deltaserve_ingest_ft`.
+- That calls `FinetuneScheduler.deltaserve_ingest`, which runs `FinetuningStore.add_rows`. New samples join the
+  current epoch's pool; the epoch counter restarts at 0 if nothing has been trained yet. The coordinator's corpus
+  total / `min_sample_len` and the child's corpus meta are kept in sync.
+- Under TP, the worker re-forwards the corpus total whenever it changes (it used to forward only once).
+- A server can start with `data_path: null` and learn only from what it is sent.
+- Gate: `tests/test_ft_ingest.py` 8/8. End to end: `EXPERIMENTS.md` rsi-e2e-1.
+
+**Gates.**
+- `tests/test_chat_sft.py` 17/17 (token-for-token vs both trainers on real formula / finer / appworld rows).
+- `tests/test_rope_yarn.py` 8/8 (0 error vs vLLM's YaRN cache).
+- `tests/test_adapter_export.py` 9/9 (TP=2 merge == TP=1).
+- The existing gradcheck / NCCL / hook gates unchanged.
+- End to end: `EXPERIMENTS.md` rsi-ace-1.
