+## Stage LC — 16K long context on Qwen3-32B TP4 + the FT-adapter slot fix (2026-10-12)
+
+**Bug fix (affects every run with `profile_on_launch: false`).**
+`vllm/v1/worker/gpu_worker.py` — new `Worker._repin_ft_served_lora()`, called at the end of
+`compile_or_warm_up_model`.
+- vLLM's warmup and graph capture end in `remove_all_adapters()`, which also dropped the FT adapter
+  pinned (and shared with the backward) in `_maybe_share_ft_served_lora`.
+- The FT adapter was then lazily re-loaded into whichever slot was free. With the inference adapter
+  already in the shared slot, the backward published into the inference adapter's slot, and FT
+  forwards read the initial weights: no learning, and the inference adapter silently overwritten.
+- The launch profiling pass hid it, because its FT requests re-activate the FT adapter into slot 0 first.
+- Now the FT adapter is re-added and re-pinned before serving starts, and a mismatch with the shared
+  slot raises. `_maybe_share_ft_served_lora` records `_ft_lora_request` / `_ft_served_slot`.
+
+**Long-context FT** (inert unless configured; short samples take the old code paths):
+- `vllm/config/finetune.py` adds two knobs:
+  - `backward_batch_tokens` (0 = capacity): decouples the backward batch from the buffer capacity.
+  - `backward_cuda_graph_max_tokens` (0 = buffer): the graph capture rows; bigger backwards run eager.
+- `deltaserve/coordinator.py`:
+  - New `batch_tokens` and `batch_tokens_of()`.
+  - `space_remaining()` offers the full capacity to an EMPTY buffer and tops a non-empty one up to
+    `batch_tokens` only.
+- `deltaserve/ft_scheduler.py`: the second and later samples in a step also stay within `batch_tokens`.
+  `gpu_worker.py` sets `batch_tokens` on the worker coordinator.
+- `vllm/v1/core/sched/scheduler.py` (two sites): FT requests skip `long_prefill_token_threshold`
+  (they must prefill in one step). Inference chunks stay capped.
+- `deltaserve/bwd_services/common/attention.py`: query-chunked forward/backward when the per-sample
+  fp32 `[Hq, L, L]` scores would exceed `DSERVE_ATTN_SCORES_BYTES` (512 MB). Each query block sees only
+  keys `0..block_end`, which is the same math. 16K on a 32B TP4 shard: 125 ms/layer, +3.5 GiB peak
+  (the dense path would need ~64 GiB).
+- `deltaserve/bwd_services/common/head.py`: streaming head (online logsumexp over vocab chunks) above
+  `DSERVE_HEAD_LOGITS_BYTES` (2 GiB) of fp32 logits.
+- `deltaserve/bwd_services/common/trainer.py` + `ft_meta.py`: graphs captured at
+  `backward_cuda_graph_max_tokens`; `process_backward` runs a whole cycle eager when `n` exceeds it.
+
+**Gates:**
+- `tests/test_long_context_backward.py`: 26/26.
+- The 4 backward gradcheck suites (816 cases) pass both by default and forced onto the long paths
+  (`DSERVE_ATTN_SCORES_BYTES=2048 DSERVE_HEAD_LOGITS_BYTES=0`).
+- `tests/test_tp_bucket_optional_lora.py`: 49/49.
+- Runs are recorded in `EXPERIMENTS.md` (lc16k-a/b). Qwen3-32B TP4, 1.2K–14.9K-token samples:
+  14,867 tokens → 9.4 s eager; every batch's loss lower in epoch 1 than epoch 0.
+
+**Memory note:** vLLM's `gpu_memory_utilization` budget does NOT include the activation buffers.
+At 16K they are ~58 GB/rank on Qwen3-32B TP4 (all saves on), so the 16K YAML uses 0.42.
+
